$ eu5-orchestrator blueprint evaluate --project /home/jan/development/ProsperOrPerishConstructor/constructor.toml --building pp_logistics_infrastructure_priority
carrier_inn [carrier_inn]
  Columns:
    input, output, profit: monthly gold values at parser base prices; input includes base worker food cost when food data is supplied.
    profit/bldg: monthly profit for the whole building when this method is selected in its slot and best-profit methods fill other slots.
    goods: direct goods input cost before worker food.
    margin: profit divided by input cost.
    efficiency: output multiplier used by the evaluator.
    raw_inputs: count of input goods classified as raw materials.
    input/1k, output/1k, base/1k: values normalized per 1k employed workers.
    amort_months: months for building cost to be repaid by monthly profit.
    rules: unallowed rule failures that need fixing; ok means no hard failures.
    exceptions: rule breaches allowed by blueprint-local exceptions; - means none used.
  Rules:
    profit margin: margin low/high when outside -30% to 30%.
    throughput: input/output low/high when monthly gold per 1k workers misses the pop-and-age target by more than 30%.
    food50/food100/food150: allocated worker food cost at 50%, 100%, and 150% base food price.
  method                                    age  input  goods  output  profit  profit/bldg  margin  eff  raw  in/1k  out/1k  base/1k  amort_mo  food50  food100  food150  rules  exceptions     
